# Global button — OriginButton

All site CTAs (hero, footer, All projects / All thoughts, About the project, forms, pricing, services) use **one** component: `OriginButton` from `components/ui/origin-button.tsx`.

Change `components/ui/origin-button.tsx` + `.origin-button` in `app/globals.css` → every CTA updates.

Rest: **square corners** (`border-radius: 0`). **Uppercase** label. **Default:** transparent fill, white border + type with `mix-blend-mode: difference` (negative / adaptive contrast). **Hover:** solid fill — black bg + white type on light surfaces; white bg + black type on dark bands (hero, footer, support-know, case hero, mobile About sheet) — **instant cut** (`transition: none`), `mix-blend-mode: normal` on hover. Font: Regular Giga (`--font-fine`, weight `400`).

## Use

```tsx
import { OriginButton } from "@/components/ui/origin-button";

<OriginButton>Label</OriginButton>
<OriginButton href="/projects">All projects</OriginButton>
<OriginButton type="submit">Send</OriginButton>
```

Index links can still go through `FrostIndexLink` (layout wrapper) — it renders `OriginButton`.

## Do not

- Wrap CTAs in ClickSpark
- Invent a new fill, glare wipe, frosted pill, or SpecularButton for CTAs
- Restyle one instance with local CSS that fights OriginButton (no `background` / `color` / `border-radius` overrides on the button)
- Put GlareHover on these CTAs
- Use `InteractiveHoverButton` for new work (legacy wrapper only)

## Exceptions

**Header / nav chrome** stays as-is: logo, primary nav, Menu / Close.

Not OriginButton: filter pills, FAQ tabs, WeChat QR trigger / backdrop, panel Close, mobile menu list.
